{
    "$comment": "Every spelling v3 renames or removes, transcribed from the two tables in docs/adr/0005-v3-configuration-and-cli-naming.md, plus the spellings that ADR names in prose rather than in a table cell. Checked by tests/Unit/Compatibility/V3RenameRegistryTest.php. This is the other direction of the deprecation registry: v2-deprecations.json is scanned code-first (issue #499), so a rename that simply never calls Deprecations::notice() is invisible to it. This file is scanned ADR-first, so it is not. A v3 rename PR stages its entries here and in the registry in the same change; see docs/versioning.md#deprecation-policy.",
    "format_version": 1,
    "$unstaged_count": "Old spellings that still have no deprecation staged. This is a ratchet: it may go down, never up. When it reaches 0 every v3 rename has shipped its notice, and the final v2 minor can be cut. Entries with channel `unchanged-spelling` are not counted — nothing about them is removed.",
    "unstaged_count": 53,
    "$channels": {
        "deprecation": "The old spelling stops working in `removed_in`. Routed through Studio\\Gesso\\Internal\\Deprecations (E_USER_DEPRECATED); `deprecation_id` links to the matching v2-deprecations.json entry, and is null until the owning issue stages it.",
        "accepted-spelling": "The old spelling keeps working through `removed_in`. Routed through Studio\\Gesso\\Internal\\LegacyIdentity's `[Gesso]` E_USER_WARNING channel instead, because a suite running failOnDeprecation must not fail for spelling a name that still works (docs/versioning.md#renamed-spellings-still-accepted).",
        "unchanged-spelling": "The spelling itself survives v3 unchanged. Listed because the ADR table names it, so the gate can account for every row; nothing is staged and nothing is counted."
    },
